35,2,1,talk,Misaki,,"@Yumi, the data is stark. Two key administrators retire this year, and the last hiring took eleven months. We are losing the people who hold the system together.","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Kenji,,"@Yumi, that’s scary! My yard scanners are old, and the 2021 trial failed fast. Plus, peak season has no freeze window. We need a vendor that works with our messy hardware!","{""words"":31,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Toshio,,"@Yumi, the invoices confirm my fear. Bundled prices held, but add-ons climbed yearly. Capital requests were trimmed, yet operating lines passed unchallenged. The true cost is recurring, not upfront.","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[""Yumi""],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Yumi,,"@Misaki, that’s terrifying! Two days unowned is unacceptable. With two admins retiring, we need a vendor who actually takes responsibility, not just passes the buck.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Misaki""],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"@Toshio, the skipped upgrades confirm my fear. The system decays because we lack the bandwidth to fix it. We need a vendor who respects that reality, not one who demands a perfect environment.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Toshio""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Misaki,,"@Benjamin, you are right. The decay is real. But my data shows the supervisors already ignore standard training. We need a vendor that fits their existing habits, not one that demands a reset.","{""words"":33,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, exactly! The 2021 trial failed because it ignored our messy hardware. We need a vendor that works with our old scanners, not against them.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
